<p>The UN Security Council adopted a Bahrain-led resolution demanding Iran immediately stop missile and drone attacks on Gulf states and Jordan, warning the strikes threaten international peace and security. The measure passed 13-0, with China and Russia abstaining. Al-Monitor reported the adopted text did not mention earlier US or Israeli strikes on Iran. Dawn reported the attacks have targeted US assets and bases in Gulf countries. Dawn also described them as retaliation after US and Israeli strikes on Iran that began on February 28, and reported that Iran’s Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei was assassinated in that period. Iran rejected the council’s move as politically motivated. Its UN ambassador condemned the resolution and objected to what Tehran sees as an unbalanced approach.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Tqn5qoxaQV5vOJ_69ndvIuTS1hKALOyKTx6SIuWiHUu6Dqwc7c3Fxe4GDP0tDDmWUEAITbfY1zm7vawskJN2BSSuoRvi5txXw-fvUM99AXJN' alt='Members of the United Nations Security Council vote on a draft resolution during a meeting on the situation in the Middle East at the United Nations headquarters on March 11, 2026 in New York City.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Record co-sponsors: The draft was co-sponsored by 135 countries, described as a Security Council record that topped the previous high of 134 co-sponsors for Resolution 2177 (2014) on Ebola.</li><li>Alternate draft fails: The New York Times reported that a Russian proposal calling for an end to the war—without naming parties or assigning blame—was rejected.</li><li>Pakistan stance: Pakistan backed the Bahrain-led text as a co-sponsor and voted in favour, saying it is “not immune from these attacks”.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Iran (UN ambassador): Iran’s ambassador called the resolution a “blatant misuse” of the Security Council and objected to what Tehran sees as an unbalanced approach. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/un-security-council-demands-iran-halt-attacks-gulf-states'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Gulf Cooperation Council sponsors: The Bahrain-led, GCC-drafted initiative described Iran’s strikes as a breach of international law and urged the council to demand an immediate halt, while also acknowledging regional mediation aimed at dialogue. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1981123/unsc-adopts-resolution-against-irans-attacks-on-gulf-nations-tehran-decries-blatant-misuse-of-security-council'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>China and Russia: China and Russia were the only two Security Council members not to back the text. The New York Times reported Russia also put forward an alternative draft calling for an end to the war without naming parties or assigning blame, which was rejected. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/12/un-security-council-adopts-resolution-condemning-irans-attacks-in-the-gulf'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>UN Security Council (majority view): Council members who backed the text said the attacks breach international law and pose a “serious threat to international peace and security”. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-war-un-demands-iran-stop-attacks-on-gulf-nations-11202846#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/un-security-council-demands-iran-halt-attacks-gulf-states'>UN Security Council demands Iran halt attacks on Gulf states</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1981123/unsc-adopts-resolution-against-irans-attacks-on-gulf-nations-tehran-decries-blatant-misuse-of-security-council'>UNSC adopts resolution against Iran’s attacks on Gulf nations; Tehran decries ‘blatant misuse’ of Security Council</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/12/un-security-council-adopts-resolution-condemning-irans-attacks-in-the-gulf'>UN Security Council adopts resolution condemning Iran’s attacks in the Gulf</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-war-un-demands-iran-stop-attacks-on-gulf-nations-11202846#publisher=newsstand'>&quot;Serious Threat To Peace&quot;: UN Demands Iran Stop Attacks On Gulf Nations</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/un-security-council-demands-iran-halt-attacks-on-gulf-states/article70732671.ece'>UN Security Council demands Iran halt attacks on Gulf nations</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/11/world/middleeast/un-security-council-condemns-iran-strikes.html'>U.N. Security Council Condemns Iran’s Retaliatory Strikes in the Middle East</a> - nytimes.com</li></ul>